DESCRIPTION:\nSleep Out for the Homeless\nThe Eta Chapter of Phi Beta Sigm
 a Fraternity\, Inc. is proud to present “Sleep Out for the Homeless\,” a 
 community service and awareness event focused on supporting individuals e
 xperiencing homelessness in our community.\nThroughout the event\, member
 s and participants will collect non-perishable food items\, clothing\, hy
 giene products\, blankets\, and other essential supplies that can be dona
 ted to individuals and organizations serving those in need. The goal is n
 ot only to collect donations\, but also to bring awareness to the realiti
 es and challenges that people experiencing homelessness face every day.\n
 As part of the experience\, participants will spend the night outdoors wi
 th limited comforts to gain a greater understanding of what it can feel l
 ike to lack access to a safe\, comfortable place to sleep. While we recog
 nize that one night cannot fully recreate the experience of homelessness\
 , the event is designed to encourage empathy\, awareness\, compassion\, a
 nd action.\n“Sleep Out for the Homeless” is an opportunity for the Eta Ch
 apter\, campus organizations\, and community members to come together and
  make a meaningful difference. Through service\, education\, and giving\,
  we hope to remind our community that everyone deserves dignity\, safety\
 , basic necessities\, and a place to call home.\nEvent Goals:\n\nCollect 
 non-perishable food and essential supplies\nCollect new and gently used c
 lothing\nCollect blankets and other basic necessities\nRaise awareness ab
 out homelessness in our community\nEncourage empathy and community involv
 ement\nConnect donations with local organizations and individuals who nee
 d them\nPromote the values of service\, brotherhood\, and community uplif
 t\n\n\nHosted by: Phi Beta Sigma Fraternity\, Inc.\n\nAdditional Informat
 ion can be found at: https://1891connect.ncat.edu/event/12985321
